# Build context for every image in docker/**. Applies repo-wide: Dockerfiles COPY from
# the repo root (docker build -f docker/<service>.Dockerfile .), so anything expensive or
# sensitive has to be excluded here, not per-Dockerfile.
#
# fixtures/ is the one that matters most: 12 MB of photographs that belong in no
# production image. vision-stub is the sole exception, and it does not get it via this
# file — its Dockerfile COPYs exactly one file (inventory.yaml) by explicit path, which
# stays honest about being the placeholder's one real dependency on the fixture.

# Version control and CI
.git
.github

# Docs and specs — not runtime weight
docs
multimodal-form-filling
*.md
!services/*/README.md

# The fixture — 12 MB of photographs and golden .docx files. vision-stub.Dockerfile is
# the sole exception, and even it does not get the whole tree back: these three lines
# re-include just enough path to let it COPY one explicit file, inventory.yaml — the
# stand-in's one real dependency on the fixture. Negating a file inside an excluded
# directory requires re-including every ancestor first, which is why this is three
# patterns rather than one `!inventory.yaml`.
fixtures/*
!fixtures/fleet-vehicle-return/
fixtures/fleet-vehicle-return/*
!fixtures/fleet-vehicle-return/inventory.yaml

# Local infra config that has no business inside an image
docker/compose.dev.yaml
compose.yaml

# Python/uv build & cache artefacts — never ship the host's venv or caches into the image
.venv
.venv*
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov
**/.uv-cache
dist
build

# Editors, OS noise, secrets
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Node/other tooling that has no place here
node_modules
